        "Two people each need the other's coat to leave the house. Whoever gives up their coat first is fine; the other walks out in shirtsleeves. The runtime faces the same problem with modules: someone has to run first, and whoever runs first sees the other **mid-preparation** — their declarations exist but haven't been given values yet.",
        "**Dynamic imports are room service**: instead of loading every dish when the restaurant opens, you order when you're hungry. The kitchen (bundler) keeps the dish in a separate file and brings it to your table as a promise.",
